An accepted deviation and a reference quirk.

`\ft Which may be called` newline `\fv 3\fv*\fq notes`: the reference nests
`\fv` inside `\ft`. The stylesheet does not let `\fv` nest (no `NEST` in its
`OccursUnder`), so it closes the `\ft` and stands beside it, as Paratext
writes it (samples-from-wild/doo43-1). Same deviation as
specExamples/footnote and usfmjsTests/usfmBodyTestD, which nest `\fv` inside
`\fqa` the same way.

This file is hand-written: the line break after `\f*` is copied into the USX
as a raw newline, which reads as no whitespace at all. A line break is
whitespace (rule 1 on `Text`), and Paratext writes it as a space before the
verse end (specExamples/footnote, the same `\f*` newline `\v`).

